          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:  \nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 37. Seizures currently occur approximately twice per month. The etiology is unknown.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:  \n- Perampanel  \n- Lamotrigine  \n- Oxcarbazepine  \n\nSeizure Burden Summary:  \nGeneralized tonic-clonic seizures occur approximately two times per month despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\nAssessment:  \nDrug-resistant generalized epilepsy characterized by generalized tonic-clonic seizures, with unknown etiology.\n\nPlan:  \nContinue the current antiseizure medications: perampanel, lamotrigine, and oxcarbazepine. Continue tracking seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
